<title>TOGO: Togo gets $8.5 million loan to improve phones.</title>
<headline>Togo gets $8.5 million loan to improve phones.</headline>
<dateline>LOME 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The West African Development Bank (BOAD) said on Tuesday it had agreed to loan Togo five billion CFA francs ($8.5 million) to help the country improve its telecommunications system.</p>
<p>The money will be used to expand the communications network in Togo's six main towns, including the capital Lome, and make it more reliable.</p>
